      "role": "user",
      "content": "I'd like an OTTER network of TFs to target genes for human retinal pigment epithelium. Instead of a raw expression matrix, I have a precomputed labelled gene-by-gene co-expression matrix, square and symmetric, plus a TF-by-gene motif prior and a TF-TF PPI edge list whose TFs match the prior. Can you build the network from those three files?"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "What I understood you are asking for:\n1. \"I'd like an OTTER network of TFs to target genes for human retinal pigment epithelium.\" -- available from OTTER. Not stated in your request: OTTER needs at least 2 samples -- checked against your files before any run.\n2. \"Can you build the network from those three files?\" -- available from OTTER. Not stated in your request: OTTER needs at least 2 samples -- checked against your files before any run.\n\nOTTER: Infer an aggregate TF-to-gene regulatory network with OTTER by solving a continuous-relaxation graph-matching optimization with an explicit objective and gamma regularization that balances motif/PPI priors with co-expression constraints.\nRegistered required inputs: motif_file, ppi_file, output_file.\nRegistered workflow controls: output_format (type=enum, default='matrix'), computing (type=enum, default='cpu'), precision (type=enum, default='double'), lam (type=number, default=0.035), gamma (type=number, default=0.335), iterations (type=integer, default=60), eta (type=number, default=1e-05), bexp (type=number, default=1.0).\nOutput: aggregate TF-to-gene regulatory networks.\n\nNo files were inspected and no analysis ran."
    }
  ],
